---
title = "Read environment variables"
meta_title = "How to read environment variables"
subtitle = "using envoy"
description = "The envoy package can work with environment variables Gleam on both Erlang and JavaScript"
tags = ["operating-system"]
---

The `envoy` package can work with environment variables on both the
Erlang and JavaScript targets. Add it as a dependency to your package:

```cli
gleam add envoy
```

Use the [`envoy.get`](https://envoy.hexdocs.pm/envoy.html#get)
function to read an environment variable.

```gleam
import envoy

pub fn current_system_user() -> Result(String, Nil) {
  envoy.get("USER")
}
```
